  "text": "Recipe: Zucchini Potato Cutlets\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Cutlets\nIngredients: red rice poha, brown rice poha, boiled potatoes, zucchini, mint leaves, grated ginger, cumin seeds, coarse peanut powder, red chili powder, flaxseed powder, turmeric powder, finely chopped Thai chillies, Chaat Masala\nCooking methods: no-cook, air-fry, bake\nInstructions: 1. Soak poha (red rice flakes or brown rice flakes) in water for 10-15 minutes. Squeeze excess water out with hands.\n2. Mash boiled potatoes. Mix them with soaked poha and the rest of the ingredients. Mixing with hand helps to get even flavor.\n3. Make small patties with the poha & potato mixture. Air fry them (or bake them in an oven) for 10-15 minutes on each side at 350 F.\n4. Patties may be refrigerated or frozen. They taste delicious with homemade Tomato Ketchup or Mint Cilantro Chutney.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (red rice poha or brown rice poha), TUBERS (potatoes), RAINBOW VEGGIES (zucchini), NUTS & SEEDS (coarse peanut powder, flaxseed powder), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
